@startuml layers
title Terminal — the two directions

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho
hide empty members

rectangle "stdin (raw mode)" as IN
rectangle "stdout" as OUT

package "Input" #F8F8F8 {
  rectangle "Terminal\nbytes -> Event objects\nreadSgrMouse, isEscapeCharacter" as PARSE
}

package "Routing" #F8F8F8 {
  rectangle "Screen\nhit test / focus\ncapability mask\ndirty set" as SCREEN
  rectangle "Container\nsame rules, one level down" as CONT
}

package "Widgets" #F8F8F8 {
  rectangle "Button, Checklist, Label\nstate + render()" as W
}

package "Output" #F8F8F8 {
  rectangle "render pass\ndirty widgets only, one flush" as R
}

IN --> PARSE
PARSE --> SCREEN : Event&
SCREEN --> CONT : Event&
CONT --> W : interface call\n(setHovered, onClicked, ...)

W ..> CONT : invalidate()
CONT ..> SCREEN : invalidate()
SCREEN ..> R : dirty set
R --> OUT

note right of SCREEN
  **Down: events.** One object, passed by
  reference, `handled` stopping it. Mouse
  goes by position, keys by focus.
end note

note right of W
  **Up: invalidation.** Not an Event — it
  carries no input, has no handler, and
  must not be consumable. A widget says
  "I changed"; when to repaint is the
  Screen's decision, not the widget's.
end note

note bottom of R
  Coalescing lives here: N invalidations
  during one input burst produce one pass.
end note

@enduml
